Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: qca8084: make BaseR wait non fatal

On boards where the bootloader leaves the SoC UNIPHY unconfigured (IPQ9554
BE7000 units) the BaseR link cannot come up before the port is opened.
Warn instead of failing the PHY probe.

Signed-off-by: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca8084_serdes.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/qcom/qca8084_serdes.c
@@ -429,8 +429,12 @@
 				xpcs_mdiodev,
 				MDIO_MMD_PCS, PCS_STATUS1);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(&xpcs_mdiodev->dev, "BaseR link failed!\n");
-		return ret;
+		/* The BaseR link needs the SoC PCS to transmit, which only
+		 * happens once the port is opened. Do not fail the PHY
+		 * probe: the link comes up later.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(&xpcs_mdiodev->dev,
+			 "BaseR link not up yet (%d), continuing\n", ret);
 	}
 
 	/* Enable USXGMII mode */
